00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:30.130
because if the heavy spender
feels that someone is stronger

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:33.690
than me without spending any
money, then they just, yeah,

00:06:33.690 --> 00:06:34.570
oh.

00:06:34.570 --> 00:06:37.300
This is just an unfair game.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.400
And they just leave the game.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:40.020
Yeah.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:41.062
They just leave the game.

00:06:41.062 --> 00:06:43.570
And they just try to
find another MMORPG.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:47.110
So managing the ecosystem
is the most key part

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.530
of the success of the
high fidelity game.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:54.700
So Netmarble usually tries
to manage the ecosystem.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:57.550
But as you know, so
many people are coming,

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.730
then someone will be a bad guy.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:03.735
So in this case, we
call them abusers.

00:07:06.710 --> 00:07:10.110
So there are some of the
abusing cases in MMORPG.

00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:12.400
The first case is
that they tried

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:17.530
to abuse the bug of some of
the marketing events or content

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:18.100
updates.

00:07:18.100 --> 00:07:25.360
So for example, the TeraM has
some bugs in our promotions.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.530
So some abusers, they cheated
to get some multiple reward

00:07:29.530 --> 00:07:31.570
by clicking multiple times.

00:07:31.570 --> 00:07:34.450
Due to that issue, it
made high inflation

00:07:34.450 --> 00:07:36.325
of the gaming economy.

00:07:36.325 --> 00:07:37.700
So the most of
the heavy spenders

00:07:37.700 --> 00:07:41.650
[? turned ?] very immediately.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:44.750
And the second thing is
that some of the abusers,

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:47.990
they just tried to hack
the client vulnerabilities,

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:52.150
such as the memory
hacking, or just

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:55.660
trying to send some
multiple messages to get

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.250
multiple rewards.

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:01.240
And also, the last thing is
that some genius hackers,

00:08:01.240 --> 00:08:04.390
they usually use
this leverage as BOTs

00:08:04.390 --> 00:08:07.450
to generate in-game
resources automatically.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:13.330
So some abusers, they're
just running 10,000 BOTs

00:08:13.330 --> 00:08:16.090
to generate in-game
resources, and they just

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:17.590
try to sell it to the market.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.960
So Netmarble tried to
block those kind of users

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:29.790
by using rule based model
because it's really accurate,

00:08:29.790 --> 00:08:33.140
and it's very easy
to understand.

00:08:33.140 --> 00:08:39.840
So when Netmarble planned
to release the game,

00:08:39.840 --> 00:08:42.419
they just designed
the business model.

00:08:42.419 --> 00:08:45.000
At this time, the
business development team

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:48.330
also designed the rules
to detect some abusers.

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:55.470
For example, if someone reached
out to the 100 level in a week,

00:08:55.470 --> 00:08:59.890
then that kind of player
might be an abuser candidate,

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:01.260
something like this.

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:04.200
And after the rule is
designed, then they just

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:08.130
send it to the development
team to ask some game logs

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:09.930
to check their user behaviors.

00:09:09.930 --> 00:09:14.220
And also, the QA team
verifies whether the laws

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.270
are successfully stored.

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:20.920
And after that, they will
be releasing the title.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:24.170
And let me assume
that the game logs

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:26.510
are successfully
store to the storage.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:30.000
Then, business intelligence
team try to investigate,

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:34.220
and they just analyze the
gaming logs to analyze the user

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:37.640
behaviors, and they just
apply some of the rules

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:41.110
to the rule based
model, and they just

00:09:41.110 --> 00:09:45.500
run the rule based
model in production.

00:09:45.500 --> 00:09:48.620
Then, the rule based model
will be detecting some abuser

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.980
candidate, and the
rule based model

00:09:51.980 --> 00:09:54.170
will be notifying
to the ops team

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:59.180
to investigate if this abuser
candidate is an abuser or not.

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:02.030
So ops team and
development studio

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:05.900
collaborate to investigate
those kind of user activities.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:10.370
And also, if that abuser
candidate is truly an abuser,

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:12.600
then they just block the users.

00:10:12.600 --> 00:10:18.320
And if that is a false alarm,
then the intelligence team

00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:21.290
changes the code, and
they modify the rules

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:23.360
to detect the right abusers.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:26.250
But as you can
see, so many teams

00:10:26.250 --> 00:10:28.310
are engaging in
so many processes,

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:31.850
and it takes a long time
to modify and change

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:34.950
the rule based model.

00:10:34.950 --> 00:10:38.550
So as you've seen,
there are some problems

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:41.080
to run the rule based model.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.060
The first one is that honestly,
it has the small coverages

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:48.750
to detectable users
because it's actually

00:10:48.750 --> 00:10:50.830
working on rule based model.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.250
So if someone is
abusing without rules

00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:57.000
or without some
unpredicted behaviors,

00:10:57.000 --> 00:10:59.550
then the rule based
doesn't expect

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:01.960
this is an abuser or not.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:04.770
And as you see, it's
really hard to keep up

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:08.520
with the speed of the content
updates and new patterns

00:11:08.520 --> 00:11:15.280
because mostly, in order to
retain the heavy spenders,

00:11:15.280 --> 00:11:19.100
the most important thing is
that the development studio

00:11:19.100 --> 00:11:23.790
keep continuously updating
the content to spend money.

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:29.130
So mostly, they are focusing
to develop the game features,

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:36.570
and they usually
de-prioritize to adding

00:11:36.570 --> 00:11:38.350
the new rule based model.

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:43.280
So it's really hard to
maintain the rule based model.

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:45.720
Due to those issues,
Netmarble tries

00:11:45.720 --> 00:11:51.710
to decide to leverage the
ML technologies in order

00:11:51.710 --> 00:11:55.520
to learn from the user behaviors
instead of adding something

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.470
by hand.

00:11:58.470 --> 00:12:00.780
So in this section, Etsuji--

